          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: నిన్న",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "నిన్న (ninna) — \"yesterday\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "With ఇవాళ (ivāḷa) and రేపు you now have the three days every conversation stands on, and నిన్న (ninna) is the only one that looks backward."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It is native Dravidian and short, with the doubled న్న you have seen in ఉన్నాను."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Three days: నిన్న (ninna), ఇవాళ (ivāḷa), రేపు."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
